# Round XII Track R — REJECT `Mutex[Trait]` at CALL-EXPRESSION generic-arg
# position (7th user-facing surface for `NonDerefContainer[BareTrait]`; Track
# P covered the 6 annotation-shaped surfaces via `ast_type_to_resolved`).
#
# CHAINED shape `Mutex[Speaker](Robot(...)).lock().greet()` — no LHS
# annotation to trigger Track P's reject at a type-position, so the reject
# must fire on the callee identifier itself. Pre-Track-R HEAD accepted this
# and fabricated `gorget_guard_greet` at C-emit (Round XI Track M class 1).
# Post-Track-R the up-front reject in `src/semantic/typecheck.rs::Expr::Call`
# reads the typed `deref_wrapper_kind == NonDerefContainer` seeded on the def
# by `resolve.rs::collect_top_level` (layering rule 2 — no name-matching)
# and reuses the shared `types::trait_name_of_inner` predicate.
#
# Reject fires at the callee span (`Mutex` identifier); user is advised to
# write `Mutex[Box[Speaker]]` (D36, `docs/define-gorget/decisions.md:1385`).

trait Speaker:
    String greet(self)

struct Robot:
    String name

equip Robot with Speaker:
    String greet(self):
        return "beep " + self.name

void main():
    print(Mutex[Speaker](Robot("R2")).lock().greet())
